{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c597","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07bd7-ea64-7de3-8c64-1b85523d9cd7"},"sequence":294,"recorded_at":1780531400000583,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3e3e40a0-075c-4b56-b191-88a15045a8f9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3e3e40a0-075c-4b56-b191-88a15045a8f9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3e3e40a0-075c-4b56-b191-88a15045a8f9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"cf265361-5823-4a64-bbf0-18eaea21bb25"},"task_id":"cf265361-5823-4a64-bbf0-18eaea21bb25","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"cf265361-5823-4a64-bbf0-18eaea21bb25","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-7-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md | head -n 100\\necho \\\"===== sessrepo test tail =====\\\"\\nwc -l internal/sessrepo/sessrepo_test.go\\necho \\\"===== secconftest points =====\\\"\\ngrep -rn \\\"Point\\\\|Outcome\\\" internal/secconftest/*.go | grep -v _test | head -n 60\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook diff and crash points\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 99f7d8b..2219ae5 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,14 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-07\\n \\n+### wbpf1v: session repository + event chain landed; provhost attestation bound rewritten around the new truth\\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-wbpf1v (first leaf of STORY-260830-3tq4ns, root of M1 chain). New `internal/sessrepo` (doc/sessrepo/chain/store + behavioral/crash/census tests), README section, `internal/provhost/identity.go` comment + `identity_test.go` gate rewrite. Work left uncommitted in the story worktree for the board CR.\\n+- FINDING (gate did its job): `go test ./...` reddened on `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`, which pins \\\"no production file calls VerifyObjectIdentity\\\". Session-record/event persistence MUST attest (SPEC §5.1/§5.2 \\\"MUST recompute and MUST reject\\\"); routing through `CalculateObjectIdentity` would dodge the text scan while attesting anyway, so the bound was rewritten, not bypassed: `internal/sessrepo/` allowlisted (schema gate precedes every Verify call, so provider-identity records can never reach one), every other tree still red (proved by a temporary foreign call site, then removed), exception fails when stale. Reviewers read the provhost diff first.\\n+- DELIVERY: CreateSession/AppendEvent over content-addressed no-replace blobs + atomic chain index; gap/repeat/divergent/stale/predecessor arms; first-event record link; byte-identical reload across handles; idempotent retry; secconftest prepare/commit faults (safe_retry / recoverable_parked_state, crashed commit counts as committed); local Resolve (exact, ASCII-fold ambiguity, UUID route); 34-site invcore census all boundary-driven with alias/var/dot-import/shadow plants.\\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_outcome.md` on the board task (10/10 AC rows with call sites, gate table, census + 12/12 killed mutation battery with narrowing/arm-deletion/census-only/audit-only + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows, tree OID + exact changed paths recorded there). Battery harness at `/tmp/mutation_battery.sh` (throwaway, not committed).\\n+- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (24 ok), `-race` exit 0 (all 24 pkgs, 4 groups), `-cover` (sessrepo 86.3/provhost 86.0), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` vet/build exit 0, gofmt clean, tracecheck exit 0, catalog current, cigate contract + claims selections exit 0, fuzz count 13 (smoke not run: no fuzzed package touched).\\n+- STATUS: handed off to review. Downstream bounds in outcome: single-branch chain, no reducer/name-resolution/CLI/lease-arbitration in this leaf.\\n+\\n ### 9ny4xl: R1–R6 closed — probe-availability claims corrected, marker census measures effect, catalog directive pinned\\n - SCOPE: TASK-260907-9ny4xl (story final leaf). `internal/cigate` claim tests + effect census + splitter tests + `doc.go`, `internal/catalog` directive pin, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` comments + freshness guard, README CI table + 20 probe notes, 2249 correction below. Leaves 1–5 production untouched; `claims.go` production changed only in comments; `catalog.go` production unchanged.\\n - R1: the capability-claims comment and the 2249 entry stated `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site; `claims.go:235` reads it into the availability map. Both now state what `doc.go` states: the gate reads `Available` from its input states (both postures driven), and what reaches no availability reader is the live probe outcome (`ProbeStates` feeds only `CapabilityIDs`, which drops availability). New `TestAvailabilityFieldDrivesVerdict` refuses/admits the same claim across postures (battery N-avail-false/true killed).\\n===== sessrepo test tail =====\\n    1089 internal/sessrepo/sessrepo_test.go\\n===== secconftest points =====\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:14:// Outcome is the Section 13.13 crash/restart vocabulary every crash\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:19:type Outcome string\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:22:\\t// OutcomeSafeRetry means the operation never mutated durable state\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:24:\\tOutcomeSafeRetry Outcome = \\\"safe_retry\\\"\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:25:\\t// OutcomeExplicitRollback means durable state mutated and the caller\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:27:\\tOutcomeExplicitRollback Outcome = \\\"explicit_rollback\\\"\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:28:\\t// OutcomeRecoverableParked means the operation stopped in a named\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:31:\\tOutcomeRecoverableParked Outcome = \\\"recoverable_parked_state\\\"\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:40:\\tPointPrepareEnter  = \\\"CR-MAT-prepare-enter\\\"\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:41:\\tPointPrepareCommit = \\\"CR-MAT-prepare-commit\\\"\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:42:\\tPointCommitEnter   = \\\"CR-MAT-commit-enter\\\"\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:43:\\tPointCommitApply   = \\\"CR-MAT-commit-apply\\\"\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:44:\\tPointRollbackEnter = \\\"CR-MAT-rollback-enter\\\"\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:55:\\toutcome Outcome\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:68:// Point names the fired crash point.\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:69:func (fault *Fault) Point() string { return fault.point }\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:71:// Outcome classifies the fired crash point into the Section 13.13\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:73:func (fault *Fault) Outcome() Outcome { return fault.outcome }\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:75:// Classify maps a crash point to its required outcome. Points before\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:80:func Classify(point string) (Outcome, error) {\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:82:\\tcase PointPrepareEnter:\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:83:\\t\\treturn OutcomeSafeRetry, nil\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:84:\\tcase PointPrepareCommit, PointCommitEnter, PointRollbackEnter:\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:85:\\t\\treturn OutcomeExplicitRollback, nil\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:86:\\tcase PointCommitApply:\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:87:\\t\\treturn OutcomeRecoverableParked, nil\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:172:\\tOutcome     Outcome\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:227:\\tif err := transactor.injector.MaybeFail(PointPrepareEnter); err != nil {\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:248:\\tif err := transactor.injector.MaybeFail(PointPrepareCommit); err != nil {\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:252:\\treceipt := Receipt{OperationID: operationID, BodyDigest: digest, Outcome: OutcomeSafeRetry, Bytes: append([]byte(nil), body...)}\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:278:\\tif err := transactor.injector.MaybeFail(PointCommitEnter); err != nil {\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:304:\\tif err := transactor.injector.MaybeFail(PointCommitApply); err != nil {\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:305:\\t\\treceipt.Outcome = OutcomeRecoverableParked\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:312:\\treceipt.Outcome = OutcomeExplicitRollback\\ninternal/secconftest/crash.go:338:\\tif err := transactor.injector.MaybeFail(PointRollbackEnter); err != nil {\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6749,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1688,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
