{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf65","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07bd7-ea64-7de3-8c64-1b85523d9cd7"},"sequence":1549,"recorded_at":1780531400003093,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3e3e40a0-075c-4b56-b191-88a15045a8f9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3e3e40a0-075c-4b56-b191-88a15045a8f9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3e3e40a0-075c-4b56-b191-88a15045a8f9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"1869d94d-462c-499a-84b4-b8775c2604d6"},"task_id":"1869d94d-462c-499a-84b4-b8775c2604d6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"1869d94d-462c-499a-84b4-b8775c2604d6","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-07\n7|\n8|### wbpf1v: session repository + event chain landed; provhost attestation bound rewritten around the new truth\n9|- SCOPE: TASK-260830-wbpf1v (first leaf of STORY-260830-3tq4ns, root of M1 chain). New `internal/sessrepo` (doc/sessrepo/chain/store + behavioral/crash/census tests), README section, `internal/provhost/identity.go` comment + `identity_test.go` gate rewrite. Work left uncommitted in the story worktree for the board CR.\n10|- FINDING (gate did its job): `go test ./...` reddened on `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`, which pins \"no production file calls VerifyObjectIdentity\". Session-record/event persistence MUST attest (SPEC §5.1/§5.2 \"MUST recompute and MUST reject\"); routing through `CalculateObjectIdentity` would dodge the text scan while attesting anyway, so the bound was rewritten, not bypassed: `internal/sessrepo/` allowlisted (schema gate precedes every Verify call, so provider-identity records can never reach one), every other tree still red (proved by a temporary foreign call site, then removed), exception fails when stale. Reviewers read the provhost diff first.\n11|- DELIVERY: CreateSession/AppendEvent over content-addressed no-replace blobs + atomic chain index; gap/repeat/divergent/stale/predecessor arms; first-event record link; byte-identical reload across handles; idempotent retry; secconftest prepare/commit faults (safe_retry / recoverable_parked_state, crashed commit counts as committed); local Resolve (exact, ASCII-fold ambiguity, UUID route); 34-site invcore census all boundary-driven with alias/var/dot-import/shadow plants.\n12|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_outcome.md` on the board task (10/10 AC rows with call sites, gate table, census + 12/12 killed mutation battery with narrowing/arm-deletion/census-only/audit-only + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows, tree OID + exact changed paths recorded there). Battery harness at `/tmp/mutation_battery.sh` (throwaway, not committed).\n13|- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (24 ok), `-race` exit 0 (all 24 pkgs, 4 groups), `-cover` (sessrepo 86.3/provhost 86.0), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` vet/build exit 0, gofmt clean, tracecheck exit 0, catalog current, cigate contract + claims selections exit 0, fuzz count 13 (smoke not run: no fuzzed package touched).\n14|- STATUS: handed off to review. Downstream bounds in outcome: single-branch chain, no reducer/name-resolution/CLI/lease-arbitration in this leaf.\n15|\n16|### 9ny4xl: R1–R6 closed — probe-availability claims corrected, marker census measures effect, catalog directive pinned\n17|- SCOPE: TASK-260907-9ny4xl (story final leaf). `internal/cigate` claim tests + effect census + splitter tests + `doc.go`, `internal/catalog` directive pin, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` comments + freshness guard, README CI table + 20 probe notes, 2249 correction below. Leaves 1–5 production untouched; `claims.go` production changed only in comments; `catalog.go` production unchanged.\n18|- R1: the capability-claims comment and the 2249 entry stated `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site; `claims.go:235` reads it into the availability map. Both now state what `doc.go` states: the gate reads `Available` from its input states (both postures driven), and what reaches no availability reader is the live probe outcome (`ProbeStates` feeds only `CapabilityIDs`, which drops availability). New `TestAvailabilityFieldDrivesVerdict` refuses/admits the same claim across postures (battery N-avail-false/true killed).\n19|- R2: the derive-targets comment named the grep + size check as the fail-closed guards. Re-measured with a real empty-leg replica (`secconftest` + fuzzless `axerror`): grep refuses nothing (pipeline status discarded), `test -s` passes (8 lines), only the count pin refuses (8 vs 13, exit 1). Comment now names the pin; neighbouring steps audited (PASS-guard loops, gofmt/coverage/fixture count guards, target-match diff, elapsed grep) — no same mistake.\n20|- R3: the marker census measured occurrence while markers classified 0 of 2 mentions. New `TestEveryNonClaimMarkerClassifiesCorpusSentence` asserts the resolving arm per mention from the production predicates cross-checked against the production verdict, and requires every marker to sole-classify at least one corpus sentence. 20 probe notes added to the README CI section (one sole-classifier per marker); measured distribution negation 2 / marker 20 / refused 0. README cell corrected to \"negated or marker-classified non-claim context\". Old corpus + new census fails (battery C-old-corpus); dropped-list X3 now dies (was a survivor).\n21|- R4: new `TestSameBlockSentencesSplitOnTerminal` (period/bang/query rows, same-block negated+positive pair) kills the paragraph-granularity narrowing (N-split-X1) and the dot-only narrowing (N-split-dot-only).\n22|- R5 (bound, re-measured this session): 13/13 smoke targets print `fuzz: elapsed`; `secconftest/FuzzRedactCorpus` + all four `canonicaljson` targets spend `-fuzztime=100x` on baseline coverage and never print `now fuzzing` (8 reach mutation). Stated in the README row and the smoke-step comment with the escape (budget/corpus change moves it silently).\n23|- R6 (bound ANSWERED): the rev2 \"Linux execution unverified\" unknown is closed by the landing PR run — PR #36 (STORY-260830-1i3qu7, merged 2026-09-06) shows `Conformance fixtures (ubuntu-latest, internal/secprim)` and `(ubuntu-latest, internal/secconftest)` pass in both runs, with macOS legs and every other job green (`gh pr checks 36`, observed this session).\n24|- CARRIED (pre-existing, fixed here): `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` disarmed the generator while the token survived and the freshness diff stayed clean (reproduced: old step exits 0 on the rewrite). Fix: anchored `grep -c '^//go:generate'` pin in the freshness step + committed `TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm`; the rewrite now fails the guard (exit 1) and the pin while catalog/cataloggen stay otherwise green (battery G-directive-space, behavioral suite executed).\n25|- RECORDED (pre-existing, not fixed — traceability scope): `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` is a `bytes.Contains` gate over `ci.yml`: moving the Vet step's `run: go vet ./...` into a YAML comment keeps it green (doubly blind — `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` carries the same substring). Re-attacked this session (PASS on the blinded tree, ci.yml restored byte-identical). At HEAD before every leaf of both stories; named here beside the `go:generate` one per the rev2 verdict.\n(more lines below)"}}}
